    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d200">

                <pb facs="0188" n="174" sameAs="frus:frus1942v06/pg174"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Colombia/45: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Keith</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bogotá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-03-30T23:00:00-05:00">March 30, 1942—11
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received March 31—3:20 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>429. With reference to my telegram no. 414 March 25, 11 p.m. This afternoon when
                    seeing the President<anchor n="54" xml:id="d200-f1"/> I referred to the note
                    submitted the Foreign Office on rubber emphasizing its urgency and importance.
                    The President stated he would study the matter carefully this week and I would
                    have some response by April 8. He added, “You can count on my aid.”</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Keith</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d200-f1" n="54" xml:id="d200-f1-content">
                <p>Eduardo Santos.</p>
